# REQUEST
ObservationRef observation
ObservationRef description_observation
string observation_attempt_id
string label
string description
string color
string material
float32 x_min
float32 x_max
float32 y_min
float32 y_max
float32 z_min
float32 z_max
# GA-312. The oriented (PCA, yaw-about-z) box that Bbox3d.msg already carries stopped HERE: this
# service took the six axis-aligned limits only, so every object written through the API lost its
# tilt and the persisted map became a mixture of two geometries with nothing saying which. Same
# shape as Bbox3d.msg, for the same reason: has_orientation is not redundant -- a yaw of 0.0 from
# a real measurement must not be confused with "never measured".
bool has_orientation
float32 yaw
float32[3] oriented_center
float32[3] oriented_extents
string room_id
float32[] description_embedding
# GA-184. Whether `description_embedding` above carries a MEASUREMENT or nothing at all.
#
# The field is `float32[]`, a typed array, and a typed array CANNOT CARRY NULL -- so an
# absent embedding and an empty one are the same bytes on this boundary. The producer
# encodes None as `[]` because it has no other choice, the decoder maps size-0 back to
# None, and the round trip was blamed on the producer for a while: 190 warnings in one
# 58-minute run, logged as "still producing empties" when the message type was simply
# unable to say "absent".
#
# Same fix as `has_orientation` in Bbox3d.msg and `has_bbox_2d` beside it, for the same
# reason: without a flag, the zero-length array of an object that was never described is
# indistinguishable from one whose embedding genuinely came back empty, and absence read
# as a measurement is the defect class this review keeps finding.
bool has_description_embedding
# One detection view's map-frame voxel evidence for the reconstructed box.
bool has_fusion_voxels
string fusion_view_id
float32 fusion_voxel_size_m
int32[] fusion_voxel_keys
# Runtime image appearance vector from CLIP ViT-B/32. This is distinct from the
# text/description embedding above and from the offline HOV-SG evaluation vector.
bool has_clip_embedding
float32[] clip_embedding
bool in_exploration
---
# RESPONSE
bool success
string object_id      # label#uuid assegnato
string message
string mutation_event_id
string mutation_state
uint64 object_revision
uint64 geometry_epoch
